Azure Techlead 
@lululemon
 | Roman Kiprin I have recently been exploring the concept of "vibe coding." While the term may seem contradictory, this approach can sometimes lead to unpredictable results. To mitigate this, I have found the Get-Shit-Done (GSD) system by TACHES to be invaluable. It is a framework of metaprompts built on two core principles: specification-driven development and maintaining current context within a file. However, the original GSD was designed for Claude Code. While that tool is excellent, I personally prefer OpenCode. Consequently, I adapted the GSD system for OpenCode over the weekend. You can view the project here: https://lnkd.in/ggKVNR5D Alternatively, you can install it immediately using a single command: $ npx gsd-opencode While I have not yet tested every edge case, the core functionality works perfectly. Any feedback or contributions would be greatly appreciated.

