hot take: pickleball didn't just disrupt tennis. it quietly killed fast-fashion party wear in KL. walk around publika or bangsar on a weekend. heels, club wear, stiff denim: out. athleisure is the default social uniform now. lululemon, alo, decathlon, the works! i now can spot them from afar. (my corporate buddies even wear lululemon to their office now cos it lowkey looks like formal pants!) finally in my era. i've been walking around in workout gear for years just cos it's more comfy, and now it's somehow in trend lol. (no more judgy looks when I walk around town) and the shoe hierarchy also sings a similar tune. my own rotation went 
@ASICS_JP
 → 
@hoka
 → 
@on_running
, and turns out that's also the exact ranking of who's growing fastest: •⁠ ⁠⁠asics: record €4.79b last year, +19.5% (the gel-kayano comeback is imba. used to swear by the Nimbus and Kayano) •⁠ ⁠⁠hoka: $2.23b, +23.6% (Clifton 10 felt like running on clouds) •⁠ ⁠⁠on: CHF 3b, +30%. (my current fave, and the Cloudsurfer Next lowkey looks like a solana-branded shoe) meanwhile 
@Nike
, the supposed OG, got lapped by two brands most people couldn't spell 5 years ago. even the malls moved. dead retail reborn as athleisure floors and pickleball/tennis machine venues. Fila just turned part of their space in the mall into an indoor tennis ball machine court. the retail dollars moved from friday night drinks to saturday morning dinks. want to see where consumer money is actually moving in this fitness boom? check it out - people are wearing it! anyway, shill me your fave brands, esp shoes! i've a collapsed arch (so sad), so always looking for a good pair to try!

