I’m standing up for my friend 
@GuntherEagleman
. I’ve known him since I had 5,000 followers. He supported me when I was small, when most people didn’t. There was no agenda. He just said he liked my content. Ngl, I was flattered. He also isn’t a creeper. I can’t say the same for every guy out there. That video supposedly showing him asking for money for reposts could be faked in five minutes with his name, profile picture, and a fake account. Don’t be naive, go try it for yourself. There is no universe where I could possibly help Gunther with his account. He is more than 10x my size. He has never asked me for money, and he has reposted me more than once without me asking or expecting anything in return. Also, I am cheap AF. I have not, and will not ever, pay for a repost. Even if you’re cynical, do the math on the economics. If you know anything about monetization, you will realize this doesn’t work financially. Digital fool’s gold. Also, has anyone noticed that internet gossip always seems to hit the same people? All of this smells like DNC payments. Be skeptical of the people who are being critical about this. Not every big account is a saint. But Gunther is my friend, and I’m not changing my mind about him because of gossip. P.S. If you’re going to shoot the king, you’d better kill him. A fake video isn’t even an ER visit.

