One of the biggest brands on Shopify is invisible in ChatGPT. I ran the single most obvious query in the category, "best gym leggings," through both AI discovery systems this morning. Shopify Catalog (UCP): 
@Gymshark
 ranked #1. Mentioned. Answer returned in 0.6 seconds. ChatGPT: not found, not mentioned, not cited. It recommended the Lululemon Wunder Train High-Rise Tight instead. The interesting part is the sources. ChatGPT built its answer from Good Housekeeping, Tom's Guide, Verywell Fit, Women's Health and Shape, then pulled product pages from Lululemon, Nike, Under Armour and Sweaty Betty. Editorial roundups first, brand pages second. So these are two entirely separate games. UCP reads structured product data. Clean specs, proper product types, good catalog hygiene, and you can rank. ChatGPT reads what publishers wrote about you. No editorial footprint, no mention, no matter how good your catalog is. If Gymshark can get shut out of the biggest query in their own category, a smaller store has no chance by accident. You have to work both.
